.TH auto-mark-install-from-source 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-mark-install-from-source - Mark a port for install/update

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-mark-install-from-source --list|category/port[@flavor] reason when
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
--list          Don't mark a port, but list those already marked
category/port   Port to be installed from source
reason          Comment stating why source build is being used
when            "newer" or "always"
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-mark-install-from-source
command marks a port to be rebuilt from source by auto-update-system.
This causes auto-update-system(8) to rebuild and reinstall the port
from source following the ports tree update.  This may be done
every time auto-update-system is run, or only when a newer version
of the port is available.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-mark-install-from-source --list
auto-mark-install-from-source wip/auto-admin WIP newer
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), auto-mark-package-critical(8)

